*>=================================================================================
*> START OF METHOD - STOCKMTValidate
*>                                               NOT Called??     so THIS NEEDS 2 B near top of called stack!
*> This method checks call sequence for logical validity (Can't WRITE if Opened INPUT, etc.)
*>
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 program-ID. STOCKMTValidate.
*> METHOD-ID. STOCKMTValidate AS "STOCKMTValidate".
 ENVIRONMENT     DIVISION.
 DATA            DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
*>
*> These are the valid possibilities... (These are laid down by the
*> COBOL Standard)  CORRECTED for migration to OC due to tabbing - 31/3/12
*>
*> ACCESS MODE   I-O Verb             OPEN MODE
*>                               INPUT    OUTPUT    I-O         EXTEND
*>  SEQUENTIAL   READ              OK               OK
*>               WRITE                        OK                OK
*>               REWRITE                            OK
*>               START             OK               OK
*>               DELETE                             OK
*>
*>  RANDOM       READ              OK               OK
*>               WRITE                        OK    OK
*>               REWRITE                                        OK
*>               START
*>               DELETE                             OK
*>
*>  DYNAMIC      READ              OK               OK
*>               WRITE                        OK    OK
*>               REWRITE                            OK
*>               START             OK               OK
*>               DELETE                             OK
*>
 01  validation-table pic x(60) value
     "101001010010101000101010011000" &
     "100000001010100110001010100010".
 01  filler redefines validation-table.
     12 access-mode  occurs 3       indexed by x1.
        15 IO-action occurs 5       indexed by x2.
            18 open-mode occurs 4   indexed by x3.
               21 OK-or-NOT  pic x.
                  88 NOT-OK             value '0'.
                  88 validation-OK      value '1'.
 01  num-cast pic x.
 01  nc redefines num-cast pic 9.

 PROCEDURE       DIVISION.
 main section.
 main-Validate.
     move zero to MOST-SQLSTATE
     move spaces to MOST-SQLMsg
     if (MOST-access-mode < '1' OR > '3') OR
        (MOST-action < '1' or > '5') OR
        (MOST-open-mode < '1' or > '4')
        perform bombed-out
        go to main-end
     else
        move MOST-access-mode to num-cast
        set x1 to nc
        move MOST-action to num-cast
        set x2 to nc
        move MOST-open-mode to num-cast
        set x3 to nc
        if NOT-OK (x1, x2, x3)
           perform bombed-out
           go to main-end
        end-if
     end-if
     .
 main-end.
     exit.
*>------------------------------------------------------------
 bombed-out section.
 bo1.
     move '99BOV' to MOST-SQLSTATE
     move "Access mode, Open mode, or intended action" &
          " are logically inconsistent. No action taken."
             to MOST-SQLMsg
*>     invoke self
      call "TranslateFileStatus".
*> end-invoke     .
 b02.
     exit.
*> END METHOD STOCKMTValidate.
*>
*> START OF METHOD - TranslateFileStatus
*>
*>  This method sets an equivalent File Status in the interface,
*>  based on the SQLSTATE field
*>
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 program-id. TranslateFileStatus.
*> METHOD-ID. TranslateFileStatus AS "TranslateFileStatus".
 ENVIRONMENT     DIVISION.
 DATA            DIVISION.

 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.

 PROCEDURE DIVISION.
 MAIN SECTION.
 P001.
*>
*> Many of the conditions that can occur under ISAM cannot occur on the RDB,
*>  so there is no equivalent. There are also many conditions that can occur
*>  on the RDB which were not possible under ISAM.
*> This Method traps and translates the most likely conditions.
*> Anything else is mapped to File status 90 with the actual SQLSTATE and
*>  the message describing it available in the MOST interface block.
*>
     move zero to MOST-file-status
     if MOST-SQLSTATE (1:2) = '01' OR '00'
        go to P001-end
     end-if
     evaluate MOST-SQLSTATE
        when '02000'                *> EOF or record not found
             evaluate TRUE
                when MOST-Getrandom
                     move '23' to MOST-file-status
                when other
                     move '10' to MOST-file-status
             end-evaluate
        when '23000'               *> Duplicate primary key on insert
             move '22' to MOST-file-status
        when other                 *> Catch-all... error and meaning are in
                                   *> the interface SQLSTATE and SQLMsg
             move '90' to MOST-file-status
     end-evaluate
     .
 p001-end.
     exit program.
*>     exit method.
*>-----------------------------------------------------------------
*> END METHOD TranslateFileStatus.
*>-----------------------------------------------------------------
