*>==================================================================
*>
*> START OF METHOD - DateHandler
*>
*> This method copes with varying date length formats and ensures
*> that both COBOL and the RDB get what is acceptable to them.
*> If applications standardise on a 10 character date string (dd/mm/yyyy)
*> life would be much easier...
*>
 IDENTIFICATION DIVISION.
 program-id.  DateHandler.
*> METHOD-ID. DateHandler AS "DateHandler".
 ENVIRONMENT     DIVISION.
 DATA            DIVISION.
 WORKING-STORAGE SECTION.
 01  dateBase    pic xx value '90'.
 01  myTally     pic s9(4) comp-5.
 01  wrk         pic x(10).
*>
*> Linkage here is not really necessary as the parameters are OBJECT
*> data and therefore GLOBAL automatically.
*> LINKAGE has been set up so that a "local copy" of the parameters
*> can be viewed easily if stepping through the code.
*>
*>  31/03/12 vbc - changed for OC  as this is now defined as GLOBAL and not sure above comment applies
*>
*> LINKAGE SECTION.
*> 01  srcLength pic s9(4) comp-5.
*> 01  src       pic x(10).
*> 01  tgtLength pic s9(4) comp-5.
*> 01  tgt       pic x(10).
*> 01  outfmt8   pic x.
*>     88 slashed6     value '1'.
*>     88 ccyymmdd     value '2'.
*>     88 ddmmccyy     value '3'.
 PROCEDURE DIVISION.               *> changed for OC as all data as global in top code block
*>                    using
*>                    srcLength
*>                    src
*>                    tgtLength
*>                    tgt
*>                    outfmt8
*>                            MOST-interface-block.
 MAIN SECTION.
 P001.
*>
     move spaces to tgt
     move zero to mytally
*> check for invalid characters...
     if src = spaces
        move 1 to mytally
     end-if
     inspect src
        tallying mytally    for all  x'00'
     if mytally not zero
        evaluate tgtLength
           when 6
              move DALBD1 to tgt
              go to p999
           when 8
              evaluate TRUE
                 when slashed6
                      move DALBD2 to tgt
                      go to p999
                 when ccyymmdd
                      move DALBD3 to tgt
                      go to p999
                 when ddmmccyy
                      move DALBD4 to tgt
                      go to p999
              end-evaluate
           when 10
              move DALBD5 to tgt
              go to p999

        end-evaluate
     end-if
*> check for zero suppression in 10 byte dates.
*> RDB can do this and it must be unsuppressed for the routines here...
*> Previous use of the Fujitsu-specific STORED-CHAR-LENGTH has
*>          been replaced with the following code...
     move zero to char-count
     inspect function REVERSE (src)
        tallying char-count   for leading spaces
     compute char-count = function LENGTH(src) - char-count

     if char-count NOT = 10 AND srcLength = 10
*> src has been zero suppressed...
           move spaces to wrk
           move zero to myTally
           inspect src (1:3)
              tallying myTally  for characters before '/'
           if mytally not = 2
              move '0' to wrk
              move src (1:2) to wrk (2:2)
              move src (3:7) to src
           else
              move src (1:3) to wrk
              move src (4:6) to src
           end-if
           move zero to myTally
           inspect src (1:3)
              tallying myTally  for characters before '/'
           if mytally not = 2
              move '0' to wrk (4:1)
              move src (1: 2) to wrk (5:2)
              move src (3:7) to src
           else
              move src (1:3) to wrk (4:3)
              move src (4:6) to src
           end-if
           move src (1:4) to wrk (7:4)
           move wrk to src
     end-if
*> Housekeeping done... now we can process the date reformats
     evaluate srcLength
        when 6 *> ddmmyy
           evaluate tgtLength
              when 6
                 move src to tgt
              when 8
                 if slashed6 *> ddmmyy to dd/mm/yy
                    string
                      src (1:2)   delimited by size
                      "/"         delimited by size
                      src (3:2)   delimited by size
                      "/"         delimited by size               *> added vbc 'delim by'
                      src (5:2)   delimited by size    into tgt
                    end-string
                 else
                    if ccyymmdd  *> ddmmyy to ccyymmdd
                       if src (5:2) < dateBase
                          move '20' to tgt
                       else
                          move '19' to tgt
                       end-if
                       move src (5:2)  to tgt (3:2)
                       move src (3:2)  to tgt (5:2)
                       move src (1:2)  to tgt (7:2)
                    else *> ddmmyy to ddmmccyy
                       if src (5:2) < dateBase
                          move '20' to tgt (5:2)
                       else
                          move '19' to tgt (5:2)
                       end-if
                       move src (5:2) to tgt (7:2)
                       move src (1:4) to tgt (1:4)
                    end-if
                  end-if
              when 10 *> ddmmyy to dd/mm/ccyy
                  if src (5:2) < dateBase
                     move '20' to tgt (7:2)
                  else
                     move '19' to tgt (7:2)
                  end-if
                  move src (5:2) to tgt (9:2)
                  move src (1:2) to tgt (1:2)
                  move '/'       to tgt (3:1) tgt (6:1)
                  move src (3:2) to tgt (4:2)
           end-evaluate

        when 8 *> dd/mm/yy or ddmmccyy or ccyymmdd. For input, we work it out...
           move zero to mytally
           inspect src
              tallying mytally   for all '/'
           if mytally NOT = zero *> it's the slashed format...
             evaluate tgtLength
                when 6  *>  dd/mm/yy to ddmmyy
                   string
                      src (1:2)   delimited by size
                      src (4:2)   delimited by size
                      src (7:2)   delimited by size     into tgt
                when 8
                   if slashed6  *> dd/mm/yy to dd/mm/yy
                      move src to tgt
                   else
                    if ccyymmdd  *> dd/mm/yy to ccyymmdd
                       if src (7:2) < dateBase
                          move '20' to tgt
                       else
                          move '19' to tgt
                       end-if
                       move spaces to wrk
                       string
                          src (7:2)  delimited by size
                          src (4:2)  delimited by size
                          src (1:2)  delimited by size   into wrk
                       end-string
                       move wrk to  tgt (3:6)
                    else *> dd/mm/yy to ddmmccyy
                       if src (7:2) < dateBase
                          move '20' to tgt (5:2)
                       else
                          move '19' to tgt (5:2)
                       end-if
                       move src (7:2) to tgt (7:2)
                       move src (1:2) to tgt (1:2)
                       move src (4:2) to tgt (3:2)
                    end-if
                   end-if
                when 10   *> dd/mm/yy to dd/mm/ccyy
                  if src (7:2) < dateBase
                     move '20' to tgt (7:2)
                  else
                     move '19' to tgt (7:2)
                  end-if
                  move src (7:2) to tgt (9:2)
                  move src (1:2) to tgt (1:2)
                  move '/'       to tgt (3:1) tgt (6:1)
                  move src (4:2) to tgt (4:2)
             end-evaluate
           else
             if src (5:2) > '18' *>  src = ddmmccyy
                evaluate tgtLength
                   when 6  *>  ddmmccyy to ddmmyy
                      string
                         src (1:4)  delimited by size
                         src (7:2)  delimited by size      into tgt
                   when 8
                      if slashed6  *> ddmmccyy to dd/mm/yy
                         move src (1:2) to tgt
                         move '/'       to tgt (3:1) tgt (6:1)
                         move src (3:2) to tgt (4:2)
                         move src (7:2) to tgt (7:2)

                      else
                       if ccyymmdd  *> ddmmccyy to ccyymmdd
                          if src (7:2) < dateBase
                             move '20' to tgt
                          else
                             move '19' to tgt
                          end-if
                          move spaces to wrk
                          string
                             src (7:2)  delimited by size
                             src (4:2)  delimited by size
                             src (1:2)  delimited by size   into wrk
                          end-string
                          move wrk to tgt (3:6)
                       else *> ddmmccyy to ddmmccyy
                          move src to tgt
                       end-if
                      end-if
                   when 10        *> ddmmccyy to dd/mm/ccyy
                     if src (7:2) < dateBase
                        move '20' to tgt (7:2)
                     else
                        move '19' to tgt (7:2)
                     end-if
                     move src (7:2) to tgt (9:2)
                     move src (1:2) to tgt (1:2)
                     move '/'       to tgt (3:1) tgt (6:1)
                     move src (3:2) to tgt (4:2)
                end-evaluate
             else *> src =  ccyymmdd

                evaluate tgtLength
                   when 6    *>  ccyymmdd to ddmmyy
                      move src (7:2) to tgt (1:2)
                      move src (5:2) to tgt (3:2)
                      move src (3:2) to tgt (5:2)
                   when 8
                      if slashed6  *> ccyymmdd to dd/mm/yy
                         move src (7:2) to tgt
                         move '/'       to tgt (3:1) tgt (6:1)
                         move src (5:2) to tgt (4:2)
                         move src (3:2) to tgt (7:2)

                      else
                       if ccyymmdd  *> ccyymmdd to ccyymmdd
                          move src to tgt
                       else *> ccyymmdd to ddmmccyy
                         move src (7:2) to tgt
                         move src (5:2) to tgt (3:2)
                         move src (1:2) to tgt (5:2)
                         move src (3:2) to tgt (7:2)
                       end-if
                      end-if
                   when 10   *> ccyymmdd to dd/mm/ccyy
                     if src (3:2) < dateBase
                        move '20' to tgt (7:2)
                     else
                        move '19' to tgt (7:2)
                     end-if
                     move src (3:2) to tgt (9:2)
                     move src (7:2) to tgt (1:2)
                     move '/'       to tgt (3:1) tgt (6:1)
                     move src (5:2) to tgt (4:2)
                end-evaluate
             end-if
           end-if
        when 10     *> src =  dd/mm/ccyy or could be ccyy-mm-dd if invalid...
           if src(5:1) is NOT numeric *> reformat ccyy-mm-dd  to dd/mm/ccyy
              move spaces to tgt
              string
                src (9:2)  delimited by size
                "/"        delimited by size
                src (6:2)  delimited by size
                "/"        delimited by size
                src (1:4)  delimited by size      into tgt
              end-string
              move tgt to src
              move spaces to tgt
           end-if

           evaluate tgtLength
              when 6             *> dd/mm/ccyy to ddmmyy
                 move src (1:2) to tgt
                 move src (4:2) to tgt (3:2)
                 move src (9:2) to tgt (5:2)
              when 8
                 if slashed6     *> dd/mm/ccyy to dd/mm/yy
                    string
                      src (1:2)   delimited by size
                      "/"         delimited by size
                      src (4:2)   delimited by size
                      "/"         delimited by size
                      src (9:2)   delimited by size        into tgt
                    end-string
                 else
                    if ccyymmdd  *> dd/mm/ccyy to ccyymmdd
                       if src (9:2) < dateBase
                          move '20' to tgt
                       else
                          move '19' to tgt
                       end-if
                       move spaces to wrk
                       string
                          src (9:2)   delimited by size
                          src (4:2)   delimited by size
                          src (1:2)   delimited by size    into wrk
                       end-string
                       move wrk to tgt (3:6)
                    else *> dd/mm/ccyy to ddmmccyy
                       if src (9:2) < dateBase
                          move '20' to tgt (5:2)
                       else
                          move '19' to tgt (5:2)
                       end-if
                       move src (9:2) to tgt (7:2)
                       move src (1:2) to tgt (1:2)
                       move src (4:2) to tgt (3:2)
                    end-if
                  end-if
              when 10    *> dd/mm/ccyy to dd/mm/ccyy
                  move src  to tgt
           end-evaluate
     end-evaluate
     .
 p999.

     call "LogIt".                *> Not too sure about this as log-message not moved to !!

*>  31/3/12 vbc - rem'd these and added above call for OC
*>     if MOST-logging-active
*>        display log-message upon syserr
*>     end-if


 p001-end.
